component mc_gear "PLCopen MC Part 1 electronic gear: MC_GearIn / MC_GearOut of a slave mc_axis to a master position";
author "SyncTwin";
license "GPL";

description
"""
The electronic gear of PLCopen Motion Control Part 1 v2.0 (MC_GearIn § 4.5,
MC_GearOut § 4.6) for a slave *mc_axis*(9) that has no cyclic synchronous
mode of its own.  One instance per slave axis.  The component is the master
of the slave's SynchronizedMotion, as *mc_group*(9) is of its members: it
writes *sync-enable* and *sync-pos* of the slave every period.  A slave is
either a member of a group or the slave of a gear: an input pin of HAL has
one writer, the configuration chooses.

MASTER (*master-pos*): the master axis's position, axis frame.  mcSetValue =
mc-axis.M.commanded-position, mcActualValue = mc-axis.M.actual-position: the
configuration wires one of them (MasterValueSource is a wiring, not a pin).
The master may be a virtual axis (an mc_axis whose pos-fb is its pos-cmd).
The master's velocity and acceleration are the differences of master-pos
over the period.  *master-axis* names the axis master-pos is wired from
(set by the configuration); a GearIn whose *master-req* differs is refused
(11), so a program can not gear to a master it is not wired to.  The slave
does not act on the master.

MC_GEARIN (rising edge of *gear-in*): ratio = *ratio-num* / *ratio-den*
(INT / UINT, Part 1 p. 94), *acceleration*, *deceleration*, *jerk* latched
with it.  0 acceleration = *slave-maxa*, 0 deceleration = acceleration,
both capped by slave-maxa; *jerk* = 0 = no jerk limit (trapezoid), > 0 =
the slave's acceleration changes at most by jerk per second.  From Standstill
of the slave only (mc_axis enters SynchronizedMotion from Standstill alone),
else refused (2).  The slave's velocity is ramped from its own (0) to ratio
times the master's velocity by this component (mc_axis does not limit the
acceleration in SynchronizedMotion), then the slave is coupled: *in-gear*,
sync-pos = p0 + ratio (master-pos - m0).  The distance lost while ramping is
not caught up (Part 1 p. 94 note 1).  A GearIn while coupled or ramping
changes the ratio on the fly from the slave's present velocity (note 2):
the running GearIn is aborted, the new one ramps and couples again.  Busy
stays while coupled (as MC_MoveVelocity after InVelocity) until a GearOut,
another GearIn or the slave leaves SynchronizedMotion.

MC_GEAROUT (rising edge of *gear-out*): sync-enable falls, the slave
decelerates at its maxa to Standstill (mc_axis).  Part 1 p. 96 keeps the
slave in ContinuousMotion at its last velocity; this component brakes it
instead (a mill stand must not run on without its strip).  Done in the same
period; refused (2) when not geared.

ERROR IDS (pin *error-id*, as mc_axis where the meaning is shared): 2 command
not allowed in this state, 7 invalid parameters (ratio-den 0, negative
acceleration/deceleration/jerk, slave-maxv or slave-maxa not > 0),
10 ratio times the master's velocity is over slave-maxv, 11 master-req is
not master-axis, 12 the slave went to ErrorStop while geared.  The slave
leaving SynchronizedMotion otherwise (MC_Stop) aborts the GearIn.

COMMAND NUMBERS (pins *command-id*, *done-id*, *aborted-id*,
*failed-id*), as mc_axis: every rising edge of gear-in/gear-out gets the
next number; a GearOut is done, a GearIn is never done (Busy until aborted),
a refusal or an error is failed.  busy/done/active/command-aborted/error/
error-id belong to the newest command.
""";

notes
"""
Wiring of a slave S geared to a virtual master M (both mc_axis):

----
net gear-m   mc-axis.M.commanded-position => mc-gear.S.master-pos
net gear-sp  mc-axis.S.commanded-position => mc-gear.S.slave-pos
net gear-st  mc-axis.S.state              => mc-gear.S.slave-state
net gear-en  mc-gear.S.sync-enable        => mc-axis.S.sync-enable
net gear-pos mc-gear.S.sync-pos           => mc-axis.S.sync-pos
setp mc-gear.S.slave-maxv = mc-axis.S.maxv; setp mc-gear.S.slave-maxa = mc-axis.S.maxa; setp mc-gear.S.master-axis M
----

addf the master mc_axis before mc-gear.S and mc-gear.S before the slave's
mc_axis: the slave takes this period's sync-pos.
""";

// ---- commands (PLCopen FB inputs)
pin in bool gear_in "rising edge: MC_GearIn (ratio, acceleration, deceleration, jerk, master-req latched)";
pin in bool gear_out "rising edge: MC_GearOut";
pin in sint ratio_num = 1 "MC_GearIn.RatioNumerator (INT)";
pin in uint ratio_den = 1 "MC_GearIn.RatioDenominator (UINT), > 0";
pin in real acceleration "MC_GearIn.Acceleration of the slave while ramping in; 0 = slave-maxa";
pin in real deceleration "MC_GearIn.Deceleration; 0 = acceleration";
pin in real jerk "MC_GearIn.Jerk; 0 = none (trapezoid)";
pin in sint master_req "MC_GearIn.Master.AxisNo";

// ---- configuration
pin in sint master_axis = -1 "the axis master-pos is wired from (-1: none, every GearIn is refused)";
pin in real slave_maxv "= mc-axis.S.maxv";
pin in real slave_maxa "= mc-axis.S.maxa";

// ---- master and slave
pin in real master_pos "mc-axis.M.commanded-position (mcSetValue) or actual-position (mcActualValue)";
pin in real slave_pos "mc-axis.S.commanded-position: where the ramp starts";
pin in sint slave_state "mc-axis.S.state";
pin out bool sync_enable "to mc-axis.S.sync-enable";
pin out real sync_pos "to mc-axis.S.sync-pos (axis frame)";

// ---- status (PLCopen FB outputs, newest command)
pin out bool in_gear "MC_GearIn.InGear: the slave is coupled";
pin out bool busy;
pin out bool done "MC_GearOut.Done";
pin out bool active;
pin out bool command_aborted;
pin out bool error;
pin out sint error_id;
pin out uint command_id;
pin out uint done_id;
pin out uint aborted_id;
pin out uint failed_id;
pin out real slave_vel "the slave's synchronized velocity (ratio x master velocity once coupled)";

variable int g;            // 0 free, 1 ramping in, 2 coupled
variable int seq;          // last command number given out
variable int run_id;       // number of the running GearIn, 0 none
variable int in_old;
variable int out_old;
variable int primed;       // master-pos seen once: its differences are velocities
variable int seen_sync;    // the slave reached SynchronizedMotion under this gear
variable double mprev;     // master-pos last period
variable double vmprev;    // master velocity last period
variable double am_last;   // master acceleration last period
variable double r;         // ratio of the running GearIn
variable double acc_c;     // its acceleration, deceleration, jerk
variable double dec_c;
variable double jerk_c;
variable double sp;        // slave position commanded (sync-pos)
variable double vs;        // slave velocity
variable double as;        // slave acceleration
variable double p0;        // coupling: slave position ...
variable double m0;        // ... at master position

function _;
;;

#include <rtapi_math.h>

#define ST_STANDSTILL 1
#define ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION 5
#define ST_ERROR_STOP 7

#define E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE 2
#define E_INVALID_PARAMETERS 7
#define E_SYNC_VELOCITY_OVER_MAXV 10
#define E_NOT_THIS_MASTER 11
#define E_SLAVE_ERROR_STOP 12

/* the running GearIn ends: release the slave (mc_axis brakes it at maxa) */
static void release(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst) {
    g = 0; seen_sync = 0; run_id = 0; sync_enable_set(0); in_gear_set(0);
}

static void fail(struct __comp_state *__comp_inst, int id, int code) {
    busy_set(0); active_set(0); done_set(0); command_aborted_set(0); in_gear_set(0);
    error_set(1); error_id_set(code); failed_id_set(id);
}

FUNCTION(_) {
    double dt = period * 1e-9, vm, am, amprev, vt, at;
    int in_edge = gear_in && !in_old, out_edge = gear_out && !out_old, lock = 0, fresh = 0;
    in_old = gear_in; out_old = gear_out;

    if (!primed) { mprev = master_pos; vmprev = 0.0; primed = 1; }
    amprev = am_last;
    vm = (master_pos - mprev) / dt; am = (vm - vmprev) / dt;
    mprev = master_pos; vmprev = vm; am_last = am;

    /* the slave left SynchronizedMotion under the gear: MC_Stop aborts, ErrorStop fails the GearIn */
    if (g) {
        if (slave_state == ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION) seen_sync = 1;
        if (slave_state == ST_ERROR_STOP) { fail(__comp_inst, run_id, E_SLAVE_ERROR_STOP); release(__comp_inst); }
        else if ((seen_sync && slave_state != ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION)
                 || (slave_state != ST_STANDSTILL && slave_state != ST_SYNCHRONIZED_MOTION)) {
            busy_set(0); active_set(0); command_aborted_set(1); aborted_id_set(run_id); release(__comp_inst);
        }
    }

    if (out_edge) {
        command_id_set(++seq);
        if (!g) fail(__comp_inst, seq, E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE);
        else {
            aborted_id_set(run_id); release(__comp_inst);
            busy_set(0); active_set(0); command_aborted_set(0); error_set(0); error_id_set(0);
            done_set(1); done_id_set(seq);
        }
    } else if (in_edge) {
        command_id_set(++seq);
        if (ratio_den == 0 || acceleration < 0.0 || deceleration < 0.0 || jerk < 0.0
            || slave_maxv <= 0.0 || slave_maxa <= 0.0) fail(__comp_inst, seq, E_INVALID_PARAMETERS);
        else if (master_req != master_axis) fail(__comp_inst, seq, E_NOT_THIS_MASTER);
        else if (!g && slave_state != ST_STANDSTILL) fail(__comp_inst, seq, E_COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_STATE);
        else {
            if (g) aborted_id_set(run_id);   /* a new ratio on the fly: from the slave's present velocity */
            else { sp = slave_pos; vs = 0.0; as = 0.0; seen_sync = 0; fresh = 1; }
            r = (double)ratio_num / (double)ratio_den;
            acc_c = acceleration > 0.0 && acceleration < slave_maxa ? acceleration : slave_maxa;
            dec_c = deceleration > 0.0 ? (deceleration < slave_maxa ? deceleration : slave_maxa) : acc_c;
            jerk_c = jerk;
            g = 1; run_id = seq;
            busy_set(1); active_set(1); done_set(0); command_aborted_set(0); error_set(0); error_id_set(0); in_gear_set(0);
            sync_enable_set(1);
        }
    }

    vt = r * vm; at = r * am;
    /* the period sync-enable rises the slave enters SynchronizedMotion and takes no step: the ramp starts next period */
    if (g == 1 && !fresh) {
        if (fabs(vt) > slave_maxv) { fail(__comp_inst, run_id, E_SYNC_VELOCITY_OVER_MAXV); release(__comp_inst); }
        else {
            double rem = vt - vs, alim = (vs == 0.0 || (vs > 0.0) == (rem > 0.0)) ? acc_c : dec_c, vold = vs;
            if (jerk_c <= 0.0) {   /* trapezoid: |dv| <= a dt per period, the last step lands on ratio x master */
                if (fabs(rem) <= alim * dt) lock = 1;
                else { as = rem > 0.0 ? alim : -alim; vs += as * dt; }
            } else {               /* S-curve on the velocity difference: the relative acceleration that still rounds
                                    * off to 0 at ratio x master (as mc_axis scurve_step), reached at jerk; coupled when
                                    * velocity and acceleration both meet the master's within one jerk step */
                double dj = jerk_c * dt, aold = as, ak = rem / dt, apred = 2.0 * at - r * amprev,
                       areq = -dj + sqrt(2.0 * jerk_c * fabs(rem) + dj * dj), ades = at + (rem < 0.0 ? -areq : areq);
                /* couple now when the step onto ratio x master (acceleration ak) and the next one (onto the master's
                 * acceleration, extrapolated by its jerk) are both within one jerk step */
                if (fabs(ak - aold) <= dj && fabs(apred - ak) <= dj) lock = 1;
                else {
                    if (ades > alim) ades = alim;
                    if (ades < -alim) ades = -alim;
                    if (ades > as + dj) as += dj;
                    else if (ades < as - dj) as -= dj;
                    else as = ades;
                    vs += as * dt;
                }
            }
            if (lock) { vs = vt; as = (vt - vold) / dt; }
            sp += vs * dt;
            if (lock) { g = 2; p0 = sp; m0 = master_pos; in_gear_set(1); }
        }
    } else if (g == 2) {
        sp = p0 + r * (master_pos - m0); vs = vt; as = at;
    }
    if (!g) { sp = slave_pos; vs = 0.0; as = 0.0; }
    sync_pos_set(sp);
    slave_vel_set(vs);
}
